<urn:atm:triage:finding/AI13-QA1-BLOCKING-03>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AI13-QA1-BLOCKING-03" ;
  triage:title "Raw socket success is never a passing case is a documentation claim only; nothing in scripts/smoke/run_peer_pair.py enforces it" ;
  triage:description "The runner's own pass/fail logic never uses endpoint_closed()/socket reachability for case success — true — but nothing prevents a config author from supplying a raw-socket-probe command as a case's `command` argv and having it register as \"success\". docs/peer-pair-smoke.md:5 and the sprint doc both state this invariant as a proof claim, but require_command()/validate() only check argv shape (non-empty list of strings), with no allowlist restricting command[0] to atm/graft-facing client binaries. A raw TCP-connect script would pass every required case today. File scripts/smoke/run_peer_pair.py is new to AI.13." ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-AI" ;
  triage:category "QA" ;
  triage:severity "BLOCKING" ;
  triage:repeatable true ;
  triage:sweepScope "repo" ;
  triage:status "scope-mismatch" ;
  triage:dispatchReady false ;
  triage:notes "team-lead re-triage 2026-07-22, following arch-ctm pushback on ATM message 01KY5PKBKV5HNYMQFFYRHJTC4D. The gap this finding names is real (AI.13 sprint doc deliverable 3: 'Raw socket success is never a passing case'; acceptance criteria: 'It exercises HTTP resource endpoints through CLI/graft-facing daemon clients, not private storage helpers.'). require_client_command() (added in 219897c0) does correctly close the literal binary-allowlist gap this finding describes -- ALLOWED_CLIENT_BINARIES restricts command[0] to atm/atm-graft. That narrow closure is legitimate and should stand. However, the same commit bundled require_assertions()/protocol_assertions(), an unrelated invented JSON-emission contract (see AI13-QA1-BLOCKING-02 notes for full analysis) with no real producer anywhere in the workspace and no basis in docs/peer-pair-smoke.md's published config schema or the AI.13/AI.16 sprint docs. Disposition: closed as scope-mismatch for the assertions portion only; the require_client_command() binary allowlist itself is sound and should be kept. arch-ctm should not extend or defend the protocol_assertions() JSON contract; AI.16's actual requirement is a real CLI-driven peer smoke extension (see sprint-ai-16-offline-reconciliation.md Required tests / Smoke row), not a producer-side metrics protocol." ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-07-22T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AI13-QA1-BLOCKING-03/s13/1> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AI13-QA1-BLOCKING-03/s14/1> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AI13-QA1-BLOCKING-03/s15/1> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AI13-QA1-BLOCKING-03/s16/1> ;
  triage:openOn <urn:atm:triage:worktree/s13/2adc5fa1> ;
  triage:openOn <urn:atm:triage:worktree/s14/ef0e5e2b> ;
  triage:openOn <urn:atm:triage:worktree/s15/5a7a762f> ;
  triage:openOn <urn:atm:triage:worktree/s16/1c23ac04> ;
  triage:promoteTo <urn:atm:triage:worktree/s16/1c23ac04> .

